%description:

Tcp.adaptiveReorderingEnabled:on -- after the first late segment, the reordering causes no fast retransmission.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Grow the reordering degree (dynamic DupThresh) when SACK reveals
reordering, so persistent reordering stops causing spurious fast retransmits".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
Rfc6675Recovery::checkSackReordering() grows the reordering degree, the DupThresh in use, to
the distance of a late segment below the highest SACKed data, up to maxReordering; the
fast retransmit and IsLost() use the degree. The growth needs SACK. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, with the loss detection "dupthresh" (precondition: RACK tolerates
the reordering by time), which sends 1000000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap delays each 20th data
segment by 3 ms, so that more than DupThresh segments pass it. Nothing is lost. Observation: level 2 and 3, at 2.5 s, the reordering degree is above 3, and the signal
ssthresh shows one reduction or none.

%# parameter: Tcp.adaptiveReorderingEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.adaptiveReorderingEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAdaptiveReorderingEnabledOn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("(tcp.sequenceNo - {isn} - 1) % 28960 == 0 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").delay(0.003)
                     .describe("each 20th data segment of host1: 3 ms late, so that the next segments pass it"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                                        .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                                        .captureCount("recoveries")
                                        .within(2.5)))
        .act(action().at(2.5)
                 .describe("the reordering degree and the reductions at 2.5 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.reordering > 3 && {recoveries} <= 1"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAdaptiveReorderingEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.adaptiveReorderingEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
*.host1.tcp.lossDetectionMode = "dupthresh"
sim-time-limit = 2.6s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAdaptiveReorderingEnabledOn: PASS
